  "description": "Not just a bike model—It’s a vision of humanity’s journey from earthbound cycling to interplanetary mobility.\n\nCarbon from Earth, Ready for Mars\nCarbon-frame technologies refined on Earth’s harshest trails now tuned for the future.\n\nGeometry of the Future\nA design that hints at space architecture; sleek, angular, aerodynamic yet rugged. A geometry tuned for stability and responsiveness, tyre-clearance for the widest lines, and a finish that echoes celestial ambition.\n\nTrail Spirit, Cosmic Ambition\nYou don’t need a rocket to ride it, but you’re riding with the mindset that the next ride will be a launch.\n\nLimitless Terrain\nOn Earth or beyond, the trail ends where the horizon begins.\n\nForged from the frontier between Earth and Mars, Mars ORB is Voodoo Cycles’ vision of what a bicycle can become when technology, craftsmanship, and imagination collide. A premium carbon gravel bike engineered for explorers of tomorrow—those who demand precision, elegance, and adaptability in equal measure. Its carbon structure merges minimal weight with intelligent stiffness. Each contour is sculpted through data-driven geometry to achieve harmony between aerodynamics and all-terrain control. The design language is futuristic yet timeless—matte carbon depths intersected by orbital red highlights, reflecting the birth of a new era of motion.\n\nThe Mars ORB is more than a bike. It’s a statement of evolution—a fusion of luxury and innovation designed for those who see roads not as boundaries, but as launchpads.\n\nFrom gravel to galaxies — the future starts beneath your wheels.\n\nIt is the year 2550. Humanity has completed countless missions to the Red Planet, and on one such expedition, we encounter the Mars ORB—emitting powerful energy waves across a vast Martian dune. Its name is deciphered from symbols etched with advanced, otherworldly technology, while the patterns along the top tube are discovered to mirror ancient Egyptian hieroglyphics with striking precision. Each detail reveals itself as part of a greater, almost divine design—where, when assembled as one, the Mars Orb becomes a catalyst capable of transforming the future of mobility.",
